--@ module = true
--[====[
seasonal-wildlife
=================

Tags: fort | gameplay | animals

A windowed tool to curate and seasonally rotate your embark's wildlife. Detects the
creatures that can actually visit your fort (per biome), lets you allow/block them, set
relative abundance, and assign each to seasons via a preference/food-web matrix. All
changes are live (no reload), including adding a species not native to the embark.

Every species the tool manages, on every layer, is ACTIVE with one or more seasons or INACTIVE and
never appears. Demons, megabeasts, titans, forgotten beasts, night creatures and mythic creatures are
DF's own and are left to it.

Nine tabs: Overview (what the map holds now), Panel (every switch, the jobs, all on / all off), Roster
(active or inactive, seasons, per-layer targets, fills, the climate matrix), Seasons, Food web, Live
(groups on the map), Layers, Vermin (by family) and Ledger (every write, with undo). The window is
gui/seasonal-wildlife.lua; this script is the engine and the console.

Usage::

    gui/seasonal-wildlife            open the window
    seasonal-wildlife status         the embark's manageable creatures, layers, quotas, fuse line
    seasonal-wildlife now            apply the current season's roster once
    seasonal-wildlife enable        EVERYTHING on: every switch (opt-ins too), every layer the map has, extinct
                                     corrections, the aquarium and its native plugin; a fort's first enable builds
                                     its roster with the preset (never reshuffled later)
    seasonal-wildlife enable rotation   the seasonal rotation only (the old `enable`)
    seasonal-wildlife disable       automatic seasonal rotation off
    seasonal-wildlife preset          the embark's preset: every present layer on, natural species one season each, rotation on
    seasonal-wildlife undo            undo the last roster edit
    seasonal-wildlife groups [on|off|coupling on|off|pack N|livestock on|off|nudge TILES TICKS RADIUS]
                                     resident groups, migratory coupling (pack size), fort livestock as prey, the ecology nudge
    seasonal-wildlife groups ecology [on|off|now|cadence N]   the ecology switch and its pass
    seasonal-wildlife groups cohesion [on|off] [herd N] [pack N] [flock N] [school N] [pod N]   leaders and follow distances
    seasonal-wildlife groups hold TOKEN DAYS | dismiss TOKEN   keep a tracked group, or send it off (cavernN:TOKEN for one cavern)
    seasonal-wildlife groups layers   per layer: cap, target, groups now, mean stay, next release, leaders
    seasonal-wildlife groups adopt <unit id> ...   these units become ONE tracked group, led (harness/placed units)
    seasonal-wildlife groups clock [on|off] [band N] [catchup X] [jitter X] [floor D] [max D] [alpha X] [prior L T]
                                     the adaptive release clock (Little's law) per layer
    seasonal-wildlife groups cavern [on|off|cap N|hold any|all|off|mix on|off|trim on|off|trim_days N|trim_gated on|off|shared on|off|natives on|off]
    seasonal-wildlife groups panic [on|off] [days N] [tiles N] [mode scatter|edge] [flocks on|off] [reelect on|off] [leader male|lowest]
    seasonal-wildlife groups natives [cavern|land|water on|off | now]   unflagged wild animals as groups
    seasonal-wildlife groups apcap <N|off>   animal-people group size in the caverns (lifted during an irruption)
    seasonal-wildlife limits [formula | fixed N | land|water|cavern [groups N|auto] [ceiling N]]
                                     every layer its own cap: the map-size formula, or one fixed cap on all
    seasonal-wildlife layer <land|water|cavern> on|off
    seasonal-wildlife water [on|off|now [BODY]|survey|countdown N|status]   the water draws (Driver B); per body: groups, swimming, next draw
    seasonal-wildlife water layer auto|on|off   v7.1: auto (default) turns the layer on wherever the map has water
    seasonal-wildlife water spill [on|off] [min N]   v7.1: a water body with fewer than N (3) drawable species this
                                     season borrows the season for active water species (given back at the change)
    seasonal-wildlife water depth [full]   column depth (stacked water tiles, each at tile water level >= 4/7) per body
    seasonal-wildlife water mix [on|off] [balance X] [balance_cap X] [feed X] [pyramid X] [apex N] [cap X] [BODY]
                                     weigh the draw by what is swimming; no settings: every species' weight per body
    seasonal-wildlife water pull [on|off] [k X] [min X] [cap X] [floor on|off]
                                     prey present raises its predators' draw weight (pelagic apexes too)
    seasonal-wildlife water scan     v7.1: re-read the water bodies now (sliced; also each season, at load, a cavern found)
    seasonal-wildlife water bodies [TYPE] | [min N] [pool_max N] [slice MS]   the water body registry: each body's type,
                                     tiles, edge columns and where a swimmer enters (the map edge; an enclosed lake or
                                     pool nearest its centroid); its settings
    seasonal-wildlife roster water [TOKEN bodies TYPES|default]   the body types a water species may enter
                                     (ocean,lake,river,pool,cavern_pool; default: its raws)
    seasonal-wildlife water levels N | aquatic on|off | budget MS [stride 1|2] | retry D
                                     deep = column depth N+; land-layer aquatic entries; survey budget; failed-draw back-off
    seasonal-wildlife caverns [survey]             where each cavern band is, and its water
    seasonal-wildlife place TOKEN [n] [land|water|cavern [depth]]   place from a stocked entry
    seasonal-wildlife stock|odds|size KEY [N|clear]   a species' stock, cavern odds or group size (KEY: TOKEN, water:TOKEN, cavern:TOKEN)
    seasonal-wildlife call KEY        a wave of that one species (land: the pool opened to it; water: drawn now; caverns)
    seasonal-wildlife sendoff [land|cavern]   every gated group of the layer walks off; DF may send the next
    seasonal-wildlife roster [KEY [active|inactive]]   counts per layer, or one species' state
    seasonal-wildlife seasons KEY <SpSuAuWi|all>   a species' seasons (an inactive one given seasons becomes active)
    seasonal-wildlife classes | class <TOKEN> natural|auto   ecology classes; bring a creature in as natural
    seasonal-wildlife ledger [N] [kind] [layer] | clear   every write the tool made, and why
    seasonal-wildlife vermin [classes | defaults | <family> [on|off|seasons <all|none|SpSuAuWi>|abundance N]]
    seasonal-wildlife vermin classes   the tool's own SWV_* vermin classes (gobble) and who eats which, this world
    seasonal-wildlife vermin class <SWV_X> on|off   one vermin class in or out of gobble wiring and foraging
    seasonal-wildlife vermin edges [rules|edges|both]   the eater -> vermin edge table in force (and its source)
    seasonal-wildlife vermin census   the vermin really on the map: loose by class and species, colony sites, water
    seasonal-wildlife vermin forage [on|off|now|cadence N|radius N|budget N|chance P|cooldown N|colony W|diversity W|log on|off]
                                     vermin eaters walk to real vermin spots so DF's own gobble acts (v7.1)
    seasonal-wildlife vermin eats     forage draws, arrivals, likely eats, and the loose-vermin trace by class
    seasonal-wildlife pattern [land|water|cavern] <steady|burst|trickle|dawn|follow>   the arrival pattern
    seasonal-wildlife alerts [on|off]   drop combat alerts that hold no humanoid (wildlife fights)
    seasonal-wildlife hunting [on|off]   vermin-hunting caste flags on the managed hunters
    seasonal-wildlife sponges [now]   the ocean-floor sponge ribbons (scenery; v7 `sponges`)
    seasonal-wildlife scavenge [on|off|now|radius N]   scavengers walk to wild remains and eat them
    seasonal-wildlife scavenge natural|swimmers|defer on|off | set KEY N | keys | stats [reset]
                                     v7.1: natural cadence (found after hours, walked to, eaten over visits),
                                     carnivorous swimmers, the smaller-waits rule, every timing, who ate what
    seasonal-wildlife exhaust [on|off|now]   a species out of stock mid-season: its nearest group-mate fills in
    seasonal-wildlife curious [TOKEN resident|thief]   curious beasts stay (flags cleared) or steal and leave
    seasonal-wildlife curious reform [on|off|now] | loot drop|keep | set KEY N | status
                                     v7.1: a thief steals, then that animal loses the habit and stays (on by default)
    seasonal-wildlife v7 [KEY on|off|N | fisher TOKEN on|off | apply]   the v7 switches; the embark's alignment
    seasonal-wildlife hunters [status|readback|skills ...|pack|packradius|raptors|stoop ...|fish ...|swimscav ...|cohesion ...]
                                     predator skill profiles (0-20), packs, the raptor stoop, bears fishing, swimmer
                                     scavengers, the whole-list cohesion table and its overrides (v7.1)
    seasonal-wildlife roster build [land|flying|water|cavern]   the guild-first roster builder (v7 `builder`, on by default)
    seasonal-wildlife roster outgun [land|flying|water|cavern]   prey that outweighs its predator's hunting group (v7 `outgun`)
    seasonal-wildlife roster apex [status|on|off|now [LAYER|invasive] [force]|target LAYER PCT|cap CALM [SAVAGE]|residence TICKS]
                                              v7.1: the apex scheduler (apex groups placed from stock to a presence target)
    seasonal-wildlife roster gobble [LAYER]   v7.1: the GOBBLE_VERMIN edge table of the active roster (the vermin stream applies it)
    seasonal-wildlife roster depth [place TOKEN <1|2|3> [n]]   v7.1: cavern layers by raw UNDERGROUND_DEPTH, stocked vs eligible
    seasonal-wildlife roster aquatic [TOKEN apex|pelagic|fisher|off]   v7.1: the curated water apex list
    seasonal-wildlife roster set [KEY VALUE | pyramid LAYER H C | pred KEY VALUE]   v7.1: the roster knobs (cfg.roster)
    seasonal-wildlife extinct [status|list|on|off|TOKEN [on|off]|set KEY on|off|mods]
                                     v7.1 (R24): extinct animals' FREQUENCY, GRAZER, roles, cluster and realm corrected
    seasonal-wildlife realm <name|auto|off|table>   the embark's realm for the geography filter (v7 `realms`); `table` lists it
    seasonal-wildlife irruption [status|on|off|keys|set KEY VALUE|tokens|token ID on|off|PCT|now|stir|end|cool CAVERN ...]
                                     cavern irruptions (v7.1, opt-in). DF's invasions are disabled in its code; an
                                     irruption stands in for the lost cavern invasion as an ECOLOGICAL SURGE, not a raid:
                                     the fort's activity in a cavern (citizens, digging, the breach; wealth, population and
                                     season weakly), scarcity and chance raise that cavern's pressure; a warning, then
                                     waves of its own civ dwellers carrying behaviour tokens (crazed, rage, thief, sneak,
                                     wandering, meandering, lingering, mischief, nofear, ambush: ~10% each, one unit all),
                                     its animals agitated; an end and a cooldown per cavern; DF announcements throughout

    seasonal-wildlife perf [status|reset|keys|set KEY VALUE|legacy NAME on|off|bench [N]|census|build [LAYER]]
                                     v7.1: each job's ms and KB per pass, the worst single tick, DFHack's perf counters
                                     for the tool's repeats and overlay; the perf switches (legacy_* = the v7.0 path)
    seasonal-wildlife aquarium [status|on|off]   v7.1: the Aquarium -- see the life of your waters: a lens that shows
                                     the creatures below the level you look at, through the water, depth-faded, schools
                                     bracketed, leaders ringed; a legend of what swims there; ocean waves and foam
    seasonal-wildlife aquarium lens|legend|schools|surf|foam on|off | depth N (1-8) | fade X | rows N
                                     | color level|kind|group | waves auto|on|off | budget MS | trip N | marks N | hz N | rearm
    seasonal-wildlife aquarium install [vanilla|subtle|aquarium|clear|shallows|custom] | restore | uninstall [force]
                                     the translucent-water graphics mod, built from YOUR vanilla sheets into the mods
                                     folder (new worlds: tick it in the mod list); restore = vanilla look, mod kept
    seasonal-wildlife aquarium preset NAME | alpha A7 A6 A5 A4 A3 A2 A1 | veil on|off | probe
                                     the mod's look; custom alphas; experimental run-time translucency; a scan receipt
    seasonal-wildlife aquarium bed auto|on|off | bed depth N (1-16) | bed tint X (0-1) | bed absorb X (0-2)
                                     | bed lift on|off | bed river pebbles|floor|df | bed material sand-mud|auto
                                     | bed below on|off | bed river-mud on|off (baked worlds: rivers as mud)
                                     the floor under the water (DF draws none there): sand under salt water, mud
                                     under fresh (material auto: sand, soil or stone by the ground), seen through the
                                     water's colour by depth; lift = water below the view level is drawn translucent
                                     too; below = creatures in the water below your level shown, fogged per level;
                                     auto = where the world has the mod
    seasonal-wildlife aquarium streaks on|off | streaks layer top|under | shimmer on|off | shimmer depth N (1-3)
                                     moving water (DF draws none): soft streaks drifting along river flow, a faint
                                     caustic shimmer on shallows; `under` puts streaks beneath the water sprite

TOKEN and KEY: the creature's raw id. An id with a space or a comma ('SEA OTTER', 'BADGER, GIANT') is quoted
("SEA OTTER"), or written with underscores (SEA_OTTER, BADGER_GIANT), or as #N, its raw index (water:#N works too).

Note: there is no `reload` command for scripts. After editing this file, just re-run
`gui/seasonal-wildlife` (reqscript auto-reloads on change); restart DFHack if it seems stale.
]====]
