--        places apex groups from stock toward a presence target (land 25% of the season; 1 group on calm maps, 2 savage).
--        Animal people x0.1 and giants x0.2 at pick, x0.25 / x0.5 FREQUENCY once seated, their own body size; vermin-root
--        persons are small predators; ANT_MAN and cave vermin-root persons join the civ set (the civ flag now reaches the
--        pool, so civ_hunt and civ_prey act); animal people at FREQUENCY 0 are floored at 1; the x3 pack bonus reads the raw
--        cluster maximum; a curated water apex list (sea lamprey demoted); pelagic slots on any ocean map; Add invasive
--        places SAVAGE species on calm maps; raw cavern depth and lava guards (no magma crab on the surface); the
--        GOBBLE_VERMIN edge table. `roster apex|gobble|depth|aquatic|set`, `realm table`.
--        Groups (R7 R29 R31 R32 R35 R44 R45 R60): every layer has its own cap, from the map-size formula or one fixed cap
--        (`limits formula|fixed N`; `v7 layer_groups` retired). An adaptive release clock per layer (Little's law) lets the
--        count approach the cap, with jitter. The tool gates the caverns: 5 groups each, natives counted, the cavern's
--        species held at FREQUENCY 1 while it is full, any surplus sent off; the deep is never touched. Water bodies use the
