--        and Groups tabs. Window fixes: real group caps, IRRUPT v2 rows, clipped labels, a scrolling tab bar. Web fix: group
--        size min and max were swapped.
-- v7.0.0 — the tool supersedes DF where it manages (user, 30 Sep 2026); each item a cfg.v7 switch (`v7`).
--        Alignment: surface GOOD/EVIL wildlife is managed as natural where the embark's region tiles match (evilness
--        < 33 good, >= 66 evil, or the world_region's flags); cavern GOOD/EVIL is ordinary cavern life; FANCIFUL no
--        longer locks (yeti, sasquatch); the Vermin tab no longer lists locked species, and a stale allow on one is
--        dropped at load. The largest adult male leads a group. Every layer has its own groups at once, sqrt(embark)
--        + 1: land, each water body (ocean, lake, river, pool: own count, clock and draw) and each cavern (own count
--        and clock). The season deal is the tool's: NO_<season> is cleared on managed species and no longer moves a
--        dealt season or skips a water draw. Solitary armed hunters get NATURAL_SKILL 10 in SNEAK, MELEE_COMBAT, BITE,
--        GRASP_STRIKE, WRESTLING, DODGING and SITUATIONAL_AWARENESS, stealth_slows 0 and AMBUSHPREDATOR (units on the
--        map too). The relation write needs the hunting group present to weigh >= 5% of the prey (CAL's lowest kill)
--        and gives SNEAK 10 at >= 25%. Scavengers take remains map-wide, off stockpiles, buildings and jobs. Listed
--        land predators that fish swim (CAN_SWIM_INNATE; water-breathing opt-in) and may take aquatic prey.
--        The relation sweep (sweep): each ecology pass clears DF's own PREDATOR_OR_PREY cells between two managed wild
--        animals that the roster's web does not pair, to NONE; never a beast, citizen, livestock or visitor cell.
--        Cavern civ races (troglodyte, rodent/amphibian/reptile/serpent/ant men, gremlin, plump helmet man) hunt by
--        their guild (civ_hunt) and are prey of cavern apexes only (civ_prey: AL/AW, not civ). fb_safe: the ecology
--        never writes or clears a relation cell of a unit that is not natural (forgotten beasts, megabeasts, titans,
--        demons, night creatures, undead), so DF's own targeting of civ races by them stands.
--        Domestic prey (domestic, opt-in): the fort's livestock and pets are prey of land apexes (AL), ground
--        mesocarnivores (ML) and any cavern-layer predator, on every layer; each ecology pass relates them to each
--        such predator on the map. Sponges (sponges): ribbons of 8-16 SPONGE units along the ocean floor, 2-8 by the
--        ocean's size, topped up once a day below half; scenery, never a group, never counted or targeted (`sponges`).
--        fishers now defaults OFF: ECO FSH2 (30 Sep night) -- grizzlies and tigers with swimming written made 0 attacks on
--        river pike in 4 runs (wolves 0 too); every listed fisher already swims in vanilla.
--        gate_drain (T8g): after a release, the next-oldest gated groups of that layer are released too until at most
--        one flagged animal remains -- DF's gate condition; a released one-animal group had left a newer one flagged.
--        Roster builder (builder, ported from the desk's guild-first design, data/eco-desk/v2/guilds/design.md):
--        `roster build [land|water|cavern]` fills a fixed table of guild slots per layer from the embark's own
--        candidates -- apex boosted from any predator guild at or past 1,000,000 cm3 (R4), min then max passes with
--        a pair-fallback seed on a stall, a link guard that drops or swaps an isolated pick (a herbivore kept
--        instead when the map's vegetation supports its mass), and a FREQUENCY ladder (v2.1 base values, scaled by
--        mass within its slot, rescaled so the roster's own max is 100) written through cfg.odds, the same field
--        ODDS and CAVERN.apply already read for every layer. Two surveys back it: a surface vegetation reading at
--        load (region tile vegetation, grass-tile share, shrub/tree counts; CACHE.veg) and a column-depth
--        count (ocean columns holding water.column_levels stacked water tiles or more, default 3; CACHE.deepCols), which also floors a
--        pelagic giant's draw weight outright on a map with no such column (ENGINE.weight) and triples its slot's
--        ladder value when one exists. With `builder` off the matrix/manual roster is the only path, as before.
--        Outgun (item 23, `outgun`/`outgun_cap`, ROSTER.outgunPairs): capybaras killed 5 of 5 wolves and buffalo
--        killed a lion in the ECO suite (P1/CAL) -- a prey species whose typical hunting-group mass (adult mass x
--        mean cluster size, the same quantity the live pack-mass floor already weighs) outweighs its predator's by
--        V7.on(cfg,'outgun') (default 2.0) or more. `roster build` always warns loudly and logs it to the ledger
--        ('outgunned: WOLF pack vs CAPYBARA herd 3.1x'); `v7 outgun_cap on` (opt-in, off by default) additionally
--        caps the prey's group size (cfg.group_size) so its cluster mass falls back under the factor. `roster
--        outgun [layer]` lists every such pair in the embark's pool without writing anything.
--        Realm table (item 21, `realms`, V7.REALMS): the raws carry no geography -- no continent or native-range
--        token exists, so DF places a species on any landmass whose biome it admits. V7.REALMS (token -> realm
--        list) is curated, external, real-world data, sourced and documented where it is defined; a
--        dfhack-config/seasonal-wildlife-realms.json file, if present, overrides or extends it. With `realms` on,
--        `seasonal-wildlife realm <name|auto|off>` sets the embark's realm (or picks it from the embark's own
--        dominant species) and the roster builder (ROSTER.candidatesFor) no longer co-seats a species whose realm
--        is disjoint from it on one layer; COS is always allowed and OCE on the water layer. A species outside its
--        home biomes is still only placed where a population entry exists (PLACE.fromEntry, unchanged) -- with no
